    "done_when": "A new module reckon/_timestamps.py provides parse_utc. Its behaviour is fixed by tests/test_timestamps_parse_utc.py before any caller migrates. A Z suffix and an explicit offset both return an aware UTC datetime. A naive value is read as UTC, the rule the callers already assume. A numeric epoch in seconds and one in milliseconds are both read, told apart by magnitude with the threshold stated in the docstring. Malformed input returns None rather than raising. Each case is asserted. No caller is migrated in this node. Instead, the manifest lists the 44 functions that parse timestamps today, found with git grep at main HEAD against the code-depth census's list in docs/research/data, as file:symbol. It groups them into migration batches whose write paths are disjoint from each other and from the live run claims under ~/.config/reckon/crew/live, and states each function's elapsed-time or display policy that its migration must keep. The test passes at exit 0. The manifest records base and head arms in the armed JSON form with FAILED ids, and the head arm is run at the committed head. The declared negative control is applied, the naive-value case is observed to fail, and that log's absolute path is in the manifest with an EXIT= line and the FAILED test id.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "Add the one UTC timestamp parser that the 44 duplicated parsing functions will migrate to",
